WEBVTT

00:00:18.227 --> 00:00:20.062
<i>Well, that must have been hard.</i>

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:21.521
Grandma.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.233
It's not funny.

00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:25.442
VIDEO CONFERENCE LIVE
YURE SHINATOSE

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.693
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:28.612
<i>But I'm glad.</i>

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.282
<i>You're later than I thought you'd be,
<i>so I was getting worried.</i></i>

00:00:33.659 --> 00:00:35.827
Wait. I'm getting a call.

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:38.455
<i>Okay. I'll hang up then.</i>

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.791
Bye, Grandma.

00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:45.170
Izana?

00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:47.005
Nagate.

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:48.382
What is it?

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.884
<i>Sorry to spring this on you...</i>

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:54.096
<i>Could you put me up for the night?</i>

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:55.514
What?

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:10.571
<i>Go forth and conquer!
<i>Let there be light!</i></i>

00:01:14.575 --> 00:01:19.871
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:26.628
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:27.379 --> 00:01:30.799
KNIGHTS OF SIDONIA

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:40.726
<i>Our only haven is this fortress</i>

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:43.812
<i>Wandering among the stars</i>

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:47.065
<i>Where we tremble with impatience</i>

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:49.484
<i>Between life and death</i>

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:55.240
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:55.824 --> 00:02:00.078
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:08.211
<i>Those of us who have been led
<i>To gather here</i></i>

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:14.926
<i>Carry within ourselves the will to fight</i>

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.555
<i>Our lives shine their brightest</i>

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.058
<i>In the defense of love</i>

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.020
<i>We boldly enter the fray</i>

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:29.524
<i>The Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:36.948 --> 00:02:39.368
ENGAGE

00:02:43.455 --> 00:02:44.665
Hey.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.375
How are you?

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:49.669
I'm fine.

00:02:53.131 --> 00:02:55.342
Thanks for doing this.

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:58.887
Yeah, no problem. Come on in.

00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:00.305
Thanks.

00:03:02.391 --> 00:03:04.059
Actually, this is perfect timing.

00:03:04.309 --> 00:03:06.770
I heard a strange noise,

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.980
and I was getting a little
scared being all alone.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.234
-Are you hungry?
-Yeah!

00:03:21.493 --> 00:03:23.370
That smells so good.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:35.173
I heard that noise
coming from a different pipe

00:03:35.257 --> 00:03:37.634
when I was taking a bath earlier.

00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:42.931
Why won't it stop?!

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.102
I wonder what it is.

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:49.730
It's done.

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:51.940
Seaweed rice balls.

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:15.005
Are you okay?

00:04:36.777 --> 00:04:39.029
I can't believe you were able
to stretch all the way here.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.364
I'm sorry I scared you.

00:04:41.531 --> 00:04:43.116
Oh, that's okay.

00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:45.285
Were you feeling lonely?

00:04:45.577 --> 00:04:46.828
Yes.

00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:52.250
I started thinking about how
many times we have left

00:04:52.626 --> 00:04:55.170
to see each other, and it made me sad.

00:04:56.046 --> 00:04:58.632
If it weren't for the war...

00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:01.176
We have plenty of time left.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.180
That's why we're going to beat the gauna
and end this war together!

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:07.265
Yes!

00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:14.105
We have finished assembling
the control systems, Professor Shinatose.

00:05:14.397 --> 00:05:16.691
Good work, Numi.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.444
You did a lot of work
on this project for us.

00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:23.990
I am just honored to be able to help.

00:05:24.407 --> 00:05:28.620
<i>I didn't know she was this familiar
<i>with Ochiai's gauna research.</i></i>

00:05:31.498 --> 00:05:32.916
<i>Professor Shinatose,</i>

00:05:33.041 --> 00:05:35.085
<i>I heard you've finished
<i>our new weapon.</i></i>

00:05:36.586 --> 00:05:39.297
It is not quite finished, Captain.

00:05:39.506 --> 00:05:41.675
We managed to assemble it,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:45.637
but we're having difficulty controlling
the areas built from the ena.

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:50.100
It would be too dangerous
to activate it in this state.

00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:52.894
<i>How long until you're sure it's safe?</i>

00:05:53.478 --> 00:05:55.438
Repeating the trials,

00:05:55.647 --> 00:05:57.190
I'd say we need at least six months.

00:05:57.482 --> 00:05:59.609
<i>We will need this weapon</i>

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.987
<i>in our war with the gauna cluster.</i>

00:06:02.153 --> 00:06:04.948
<i>Proceed with the activation test
<i>as planned.</i></i>

00:06:05.323 --> 00:06:06.783
But, ma'am...

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.828
Understood.

00:06:17.335 --> 00:06:19.754
We will be conducting
joint clasp formation drills

00:06:19.838 --> 00:06:22.424
between the Mark 17 upgraded
Tsugumori and the Mark 18s!

00:06:22.632 --> 00:06:23.592
Four unit clasp formation!

00:06:33.268 --> 00:06:34.686
Good acceleration.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.857
The upgraded Tsugumori's
four unit clasp formation is fast.

00:06:38.982 --> 00:06:42.110
And the new propulsion
engine has stabilized.

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:43.278
It's looking good.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:49.784
What was it?

00:07:02.213 --> 00:07:04.257
It's Tsumugi.
I apologize for the delay,

00:07:04.341 --> 00:07:06.384
but I am here to participate
in the drills as well.

00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:10.639
I am Tsumugi's new pilot, Mozuku Kunato.

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:13.224
Pleased to meet you.

00:07:16.394 --> 00:07:17.520
<i>She is fast.</i>

00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:19.189
<i>We can't catch her.</i>

00:07:19.397 --> 00:07:20.899
Very impressive.

00:07:21.483 --> 00:07:24.235
How is she going so fast?

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:27.656
What? I'm not really sure.

00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:31.159
It would be great if we could use
that technology with the gardes.

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.370
Kunato,

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.789
you know how she works, don't you?

00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:37.332
Unfortunately,

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.584
there is much that is still unclear to me.

00:07:40.335 --> 00:07:42.087
Honestly.

00:07:43.672 --> 00:07:44.673
Garde squad,

00:07:44.756 --> 00:07:48.093
we will now be conducting joint clasp
formation drills with the hybrid Tsumugi.

00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:49.052
<i>Copy that!</i>

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:50.595
Release clasp formation!

00:07:54.641 --> 00:07:56.059
Tanikaze,

00:07:56.685 --> 00:07:58.228
show me what to do.

00:07:58.436 --> 00:08:00.522
All right. Are you ready, Tsumugi?

00:08:04.818 --> 00:08:06.152
Tanikaze...

00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:11.741
Look at that amazing mobility.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:17.288
You know, Tanikaze and that hybrid
are perfectly in sync.

00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:19.207
<i>What do you think, Samari?</i>

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.458
Yeah, I guess.

00:08:33.471 --> 00:08:36.182
<i>Tanikaze and Tsumugi's joint clasp
<i>formation average speed</i></i>

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:38.643
<i>is eight times faster
<i>than the Mark 18's usual average.</i></i>

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.061
They can still go faster.

00:08:40.145 --> 00:08:42.772
Their turning performance
is ten times better as well.

00:08:42.897 --> 00:08:44.983
This exceeds my expectations.

00:08:49.946 --> 00:08:52.949
-Nagate Tanikaze.
-Yes.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.163
It seems that Tsumugi has really taken
a liking to you.

00:08:58.705 --> 00:09:02.625
I hope we can continue to work together.

00:09:07.839 --> 00:09:08.923
And...

00:09:09.424 --> 00:09:11.760
Please take good care of Tsumugi.

00:09:12.343 --> 00:09:14.679
Yes. I will.

00:09:15.263 --> 00:09:17.140
Well, please excuse me.

00:09:18.099 --> 00:09:19.017
Bye...

00:09:23.813 --> 00:09:25.523
There's still time.

00:09:26.107 --> 00:09:27.567
All right.

00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:39.204
Hello.

00:09:39.537 --> 00:09:42.248
Hello, Mr. Tanikaze.

00:09:42.874 --> 00:09:44.084
Well...

00:09:44.334 --> 00:09:46.377
There was something more
I wanted to discuss.

00:09:47.378 --> 00:09:48.630
Yes?

00:09:49.547 --> 00:09:55.428
SITES OF SIDONIA
NEW HANGAR BAY 7

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.974
Did the map of the pipes
I gave you prove useful?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.560
Yes, it did.

00:10:02.894 --> 00:10:04.354
Thank you very much.

00:10:05.021 --> 00:10:06.564
Actually...

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:09.651
I came to discuss something else today.

00:10:10.068 --> 00:10:11.653
Yes, how can I help you?

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.406
I'm looking for a property with several
of the old pipes running through it.

00:10:15.782 --> 00:10:18.368
Oh, that sounds nice.

00:10:18.576 --> 00:10:20.620
I didn't know you liked pipes that much.

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:23.081
I did some research of my own.

00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:25.792
Would you mind taking a look?

00:10:26.543 --> 00:10:27.961
Let's see.

00:10:28.253 --> 00:10:31.089
I'd like a place around this outer wall
or on this block,

00:10:31.256 --> 00:10:33.716
and preferably somewhere
not very populated--

00:10:33.842 --> 00:10:34.843
Outer wall?

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:36.344
Yes.

00:10:36.761 --> 00:10:38.596
Here, I have this.

00:10:38.888 --> 00:10:40.640
UNRESTRICTED RESIDENCY
AUTHORIZATION CERTIFICATION

00:10:40.723 --> 00:10:44.310
This is an unrestricted
residency authorization certificate!

00:10:46.813 --> 00:10:51.526
This is the first time I've ever shown
a property along the outer wall.

00:10:51.943 --> 00:10:54.988
Let me find another map of the piping.

00:10:56.281 --> 00:10:59.117
Hold on one second.

00:11:00.743 --> 00:11:03.371
I'm so jealous...

00:11:03.538 --> 00:11:06.166
that you get to live out
by the outer wall.

00:11:10.628 --> 00:11:12.797
R... Really?

00:11:13.214 --> 00:11:15.133
Yes!

00:11:19.888 --> 00:11:21.598
Now, if I'm not mistaken,

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:25.852
pilots have to live near
the main transportation line, right?

00:11:25.935 --> 00:11:26.936
NEW PROPERTY LISTINGS

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.479
How about this one?

00:11:29.188 --> 00:11:33.109
It's an old property, but look at all
of the old pipes coiling around it.

00:11:35.486 --> 00:11:37.405
It might be too difficult
to pass through.

00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:39.157
-What?
-Oh, I mean...

00:11:39.657 --> 00:11:42.285
Is there anything
closer on the east side?

00:11:42.493 --> 00:11:45.413
Hmm... let me look.

00:11:45.496 --> 00:11:47.248
Oh, how about this one?

00:11:50.919 --> 00:11:52.879
Yes, that might be good.

00:11:55.214 --> 00:11:56.090
Hello.

00:11:56.966 --> 00:11:59.969
Oh, Yuhata, long time no see.

00:12:01.095 --> 00:12:05.767
I haven't been able to get
any free time to come out here.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.895
Is there anything new that's good?

00:12:10.939 --> 00:12:12.815
What are you building?

00:12:14.609 --> 00:12:16.152
Hey! Is that what I think it is?!

00:12:16.653 --> 00:12:21.324
It's a gravitational beam emitter.

00:12:22.283 --> 00:12:24.619
Theoretically,
the most powerful weapon ever!

00:12:24.744 --> 00:12:27.038
Wow, did you make it yourself?

00:12:27.372 --> 00:12:30.667
I saw it in a science-fiction weapons
encyclopedia when I was younger!

00:12:31.668 --> 00:12:35.755
"There is nothing
this weapon cannot penetrate!"

00:12:35.838 --> 00:12:38.675
I still have that book.

00:12:39.926 --> 00:12:42.929
This really brings back memories.

00:12:49.477 --> 00:12:51.771
I'm glad you like the place.

00:12:51.854 --> 00:12:52.689
Yes.

00:12:52.981 --> 00:12:54.607
Tanikaze?

00:12:55.316 --> 00:12:59.153
Thank you
for taking me to see it.

00:12:59.237 --> 00:13:02.323
Oh, don't mention it. I'm happy
I got to see some beautiful piping.

00:13:02.407 --> 00:13:04.784
That's the Residential Administration.

00:13:04.867 --> 00:13:05.827
RECORD:
RESIDENTIAL ADMINISTRATION

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.078
COMPLETED DEPARTURE
FROM THE PILOT DORMITORY

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:11.332
How could I be this careless?

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:18.256
-I'm home!
-Welcome back.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:22.343
You got done early today.
I'm glad I gave you a key.

00:13:22.427 --> 00:13:23.302
Yeah.

00:13:24.554 --> 00:13:28.141
You know, if you wanted to...

00:13:29.183 --> 00:13:32.437
you could... live here...

00:13:34.188 --> 00:13:35.732
What is that?

00:13:36.065 --> 00:13:38.443
-A map of the piping?
-Yeah.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:41.821
I actually went to look
for a new place to live.

00:13:44.198 --> 00:13:46.242
Oh, really? I see.

00:13:46.743 --> 00:13:49.078
This is the place I looked at today.

00:13:49.537 --> 00:13:51.497
And this is...

00:13:53.124 --> 00:13:55.043
-Tsumugi's room!
-Yeah.

00:13:55.376 --> 00:13:58.880
Wow! This is a place on the outer wall!

00:13:59.589 --> 00:14:00.798
So...

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:04.677
would you want to move there together?

00:14:05.261 --> 00:14:06.137
What?

00:14:07.138 --> 00:14:09.724
You know, only if you wanted to.

00:14:11.768 --> 00:14:14.604
What do you mean, if I wanted to?

00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:15.938
What?

00:14:16.022 --> 00:14:18.649
This is on the outer wall.

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:23.196
You might be able to get permission...

00:14:23.738 --> 00:14:27.575
but it's not a place a regular pilot

00:14:27.658 --> 00:14:29.911
like me can live.

00:14:30.828 --> 00:14:32.663
You don't need to worry about that!

00:14:32.747 --> 00:14:36.667
It says right here I'm allowed
to have one roommate!

00:14:36.793 --> 00:14:37.668
Look.

00:14:38.252 --> 00:14:40.630
See, Izana?

00:14:43.049 --> 00:14:47.678
I'm sorry.
I wanted to talk to you about it before...

00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:51.474
but my schedule
suddenly freed up today.

00:14:54.394 --> 00:14:58.231
It's fine.
I guess I can move in with you.

00:15:06.823 --> 00:15:08.324
This way.

00:15:12.203 --> 00:15:14.163
Isn't it kind of far from the station?

00:15:15.415 --> 00:15:17.875
Don't worry,
there's a direct elevator line

00:15:17.959 --> 00:15:20.711
to the military district
behind the building.

00:15:23.047 --> 00:15:24.424
There it is.

00:15:35.059 --> 00:15:36.602
Wow, it's a great place.

00:15:36.686 --> 00:15:37.979
Right?

00:15:40.189 --> 00:15:41.816
I'm going to call Tsumugi.

00:15:45.862 --> 00:15:47.989
Izana! Hold your breath!

00:15:48.656 --> 00:15:50.741
She said there was
a lot of dust in the pipes,

00:15:50.825 --> 00:15:52.285
so she's going to blow it out.

00:15:52.368 --> 00:15:54.287
What? Oh, okay.

00:15:58.875 --> 00:16:00.042
Hi, there!

00:16:01.043 --> 00:16:03.546
Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:16:05.214 --> 00:16:09.177
It's fine. We were going
to do some cleaning anyway.

00:16:09.844 --> 00:16:11.846
Were there any problems
other than the dust?

00:16:12.305 --> 00:16:14.098
No, no problems.

00:16:14.515 --> 00:16:16.309
There was plenty of room in the pipes,

00:16:16.392 --> 00:16:18.895
and I was able to make
my way here pretty comfortably.

00:16:19.687 --> 00:16:20.980
Oh, that's good.

00:16:21.314 --> 00:16:22.440
Yes!

00:16:34.118 --> 00:16:36.329
What's wrong, Tanikaze?

00:16:36.412 --> 00:16:38.372
You seem down.

00:16:38.456 --> 00:16:41.501
Tsumugi, you're still up?

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:46.172
I actually don't need to sleep,

00:16:46.547 --> 00:16:50.176
although I can fall asleep if I want to.

00:16:50.927 --> 00:16:53.346
I'm a little different.

00:16:55.389 --> 00:16:57.141
Here.

00:16:57.225 --> 00:16:59.060
This was crawling on the back wall.

00:16:59.143 --> 00:17:02.730
Wait, that's a saw-toothed stag beetle!

00:17:02.813 --> 00:17:05.233
Not so loud.

00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:07.860
Izana is probably sleeping.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:12.323
Can I touch it?

00:17:12.615 --> 00:17:15.451
Yeah, but be gentle.

00:17:15.993 --> 00:17:19.580
This is my first time seeing a real one.

00:17:19.956 --> 00:17:21.123
Me, too.

00:17:22.583 --> 00:17:25.378
I like the way it's shaped.

00:17:31.759 --> 00:17:33.135
Sorry.

00:17:33.761 --> 00:17:37.557
That's all right.
I was going to let it go anyway.

00:17:38.224 --> 00:17:40.518
I'm sure from the beetle's point of view,

00:17:40.601 --> 00:17:45.481
we're terrifying predators
it can't communicate with.

00:17:47.984 --> 00:17:49.694
Yeah, maybe.

00:17:51.028 --> 00:17:53.239
<i>Maybe it's just that we're so different,</i>

00:17:53.322 --> 00:17:57.868
<i>we haven't figured out the best way
<i>to communicate with each other.</i></i>

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:01.998
Hoshijiro...

00:18:03.249 --> 00:18:05.459
Tanikaze?

00:18:07.587 --> 00:18:08.963
Yeah?

00:18:10.214 --> 00:18:11.799
It's pretty late.

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:13.426
We should get some sleep.

00:18:13.509 --> 00:18:15.428
Oh, okay.

00:18:15.761 --> 00:18:17.930
Well, good night.

00:18:18.389 --> 00:18:20.099
Good night.

00:18:32.028 --> 00:18:32.987
Tsumugi?

00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:36.324
I wanted to...

00:18:37.408 --> 00:18:39.535
I want to sleep next to you.

00:18:39.619 --> 00:18:40.494
What?

00:18:41.704 --> 00:18:43.873
Could I? Please?

00:18:47.627 --> 00:18:48.544
Sure. Go ahead.

00:19:07.313 --> 00:19:09.565
We are passing near the asteroid.

00:19:09.649 --> 00:19:11.567
Its distance is 180,000 kilometers.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.278
If we're so close,

00:19:14.362 --> 00:19:16.072
why aren't we going
to mine it for resources?

00:19:16.739 --> 00:19:20.242
I'm not sure. I thought the captain
specifically chose this course...

00:19:20.326 --> 00:19:23.746
that crosses near the asteroid
because she wanted to mine for resources.

00:19:48.229 --> 00:19:50.940
<i>Entering final preparations
<i>for the beam emitter.</i></i>

00:19:51.023 --> 00:19:53.859
<i>All crew members,
<i>please evacuate the test chamber.</i></i>

00:19:53.943 --> 00:19:55.236
<i>Heigus particle well,</i>

00:19:55.319 --> 00:19:58.781
<i>current flow control good.
<i>No effect to non-relevant districts.</i></i>

00:19:58.864 --> 00:20:00.574
<i>Heigus reflux device...</i>

00:20:00.658 --> 00:20:02.743
<i>and reflux safety valve in operation.</i>

00:20:02.827 --> 00:20:05.371
<i>Beam emitter experimental team,
<i>confirming final deployment.</i></i>

00:20:05.871 --> 00:20:08.874
So... this is it.

00:20:09.583 --> 00:20:11.293
It's just like a gauna.

00:20:11.377 --> 00:20:12.545
Yes.

00:20:12.962 --> 00:20:15.756
The capability of the ena
to be built into anything

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:18.175
allowed us to finally complete it.

00:20:19.301 --> 00:20:22.596
The gravitational beam emitter...

00:20:23.389 --> 00:20:27.309
A weapon from the mind
of the scientist Ochiai.

00:20:27.685 --> 00:20:29.729
Control, can you hear me?

00:20:30.104 --> 00:20:32.523
Connect it to the Heigus particle well.

00:20:32.857 --> 00:20:34.191
<i>Copy that.</i>

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:36.402
<i>Be careful.</i>

00:20:42.825 --> 00:20:45.870
Connecting to the Heigus particle well.

00:20:52.585 --> 00:20:55.337
Current pathway secured.
Proceeding with charge.

00:20:55.421 --> 00:20:56.756
TEST CHAMBER
REMOTE OPERATION ROOM

00:20:56.839 --> 00:20:57.965
CHARGE CONNECTED

00:20:58.048 --> 00:21:00.426
Beam emitter, activate.

00:21:01.552 --> 00:21:03.512
Releasing safety valve.

00:21:04.221 --> 00:21:06.474
Activating beam emitter.

00:21:11.979 --> 00:21:13.272
<i>It has been activated.</i>

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:17.568
Targeting the nearby asteroid.

00:21:25.701 --> 00:21:26.702
GRAVITATIONAL BEAM EMITTER
TARGET LOCKED

00:21:27.077 --> 00:21:30.414
Target locked, ready to fire.

00:21:32.249 --> 00:21:33.083
Fire.

00:21:33.501 --> 00:21:34.919
Gravitational beam emitter.

00:21:36.504 --> 00:21:37.463
Fire!

00:22:15.501 --> 00:22:17.044
Test successful.

00:22:17.503 --> 00:22:20.047
All matter within 100 kilometers...

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:23.717
of the beam trajectory
has been vaporized.

00:22:25.219 --> 00:22:26.637
Captain?

00:22:30.057 --> 00:22:31.976
Spectacular.

00:22:40.859 --> 00:22:42.486
TO BE CONTINUED

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:50.828
<i>Oh, if this world must decay</i>

00:22:50.911 --> 00:22:54.582
<i>And I'm destined to give my life away</i>

00:22:54.665 --> 00:22:59.753
<i>What should I be living for?</i>

00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:05.676
<i>If I had never met you</i>

00:23:05.759 --> 00:23:09.346
<i>I would never have known</i>

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:15.352
<i>This pain that tears at my heart</i>

00:23:15.436 --> 00:23:17.771
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-Echoing there</i></i>

00:23:17.855 --> 00:23:19.857
<i>-Fortune
<i>-In the furthest reaches of the cosmos</i></i>

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:22.860
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Is this clumsy requiem</i></i>

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.237
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-And yet</i></i>

00:23:25.321 --> 00:23:27.156
<i>-Fortune
<i>-I'm still searching</i></i>

00:23:27.239 --> 00:23:30.576
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Within this uncertain reality</i></i>

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.661
<i>For you</i>

00:23:32.745 --> 00:23:36.373
<i>The joy of our finding each other</i>

00:23:36.457 --> 00:23:40.085
<i>The vanished warmth</i>

00:23:40.169 --> 00:23:43.797
<i>You should know that I remember it all</i>

00:23:43.881 --> 00:23:47.551
<i>Because I loved you</i>

00:23:47.635 --> 00:23:51.221
<i>The emotions that arise</i>

00:23:51.305 --> 00:23:54.850
<i>The scars left in my heart</i>

00:23:54.933 --> 00:23:59.271
<i>You should know that I'll carry them all</i>

00:23:59.355 --> 00:24:05.944
<i>As I walk this path</i>
